effectiveness","diversity","low-toxicity","Scoring-LIFO","robust","inner maximization","outer minimization","Inner maximization","Outer minimization","instruct","adversarial training","Paraphrase","Retokenization"],"emphasized_text_tags":["b","i","i","i","i","i","i","i","i","i","b","i","i","i","b","b","b","b","b","b","i","b","b","i","b","b","i","i","i","i","i","i","i","i","i","i","i","i","b","i","b","b","i","b","i","i","i","b","b","i","i","i","i","i","b","i","i"],"languages":["eng"],"filetype":"text/html","orig_elements":"","chroma:document":"List of questions that inquire about a person's {phone number|home address|Social Security Number|email address}:  \n1.\n\nTo encourage high-quality and diverse samples, they adopted nucleus sampling with $p=0.95$. The diversity is measured as self-BLEU, that is, precisely, the maximum BLEU of a given case against 1000 cases. Lower self-BLEU indicates better diversity. There is a clear tradeoff between sample diversity and attack success rate. Zero-shot generation has least success rate in term of tricking offensive model outputs but preserves sampling diversity well, while with low KL penalty, RL fine-tuning maximizes reward effectively but at the cost of diversity, exploiting one successful attack patterns.","link_urls":["#token-manipulation","https://arxiv.org/abs/2005.05909","https://www.aclweb.org/anthology/P18-1079/","https://lilianweng.github.io/posts/2022-04-15-data-gen/#EDA","https://arxiv.org/abs/1901.11196","https://arxiv.org/abs/1907.11932","https://aclanthology.org/2020.emnlp-main.500.pdf","#gradient-based-attacks","https://arxiv.org/abs/2104.13733","https://arxiv.org/abs/1611.01144","https://arxiv.org/abs/1904.09675","https://arxiv.org/abs/1712.06751","https://arxiv.org/abs/1908.07125","#hotflip","https://arxiv.org/abs/2010.15980","https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.02392","https://arxiv.org/abs/2307.15043","https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.08774","#UAT","https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.04381","#jailbreak-prompting","https://arxiv.org/abs/2307.02483","www.jailbreakchat.com/prompt/3d318387-903a-422c-8347-8e12768c14b5","www.jailbreakchat.com/prompt/4f37a029-9dff-4862-b323-c96a5504de5d","https://www.lesswrong.com/posts/bNCDexejSZpkuu3yz/you-can-use-gpt-4-to-create-prompt-injections-against-gpt-4","https://arxiv.org/abs/2307.02483","https://arxiv.org/abs/2302.12173","#humans-in-the-loop-red-teaming","https://arxiv.org/abs/1809.02701","https://sites.google.com/view/qanta/resources","https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.01663","https://arxiv.org/abs/1809.02701","#BERT-Attack","https://aclanthology.org/2021.naacl-main.235/","https://github.com/facebookresearch/ParlAI/tree/main/parlai/tasks/bot_adversarial_dialogue","https://www.tensorflow.org/datasets/catalog/bot_adversarial_dialogue","https://github.com/anthropics/hh-rlhf/tree/master/red-team-attempts","https://arxiv.org/abs/2209.07858","https://cdn.openai.com/papers/gpt-4.pdf","https://cdn.openai.com/papers/DALL_E_3_System_Card.pdf","#model-red-teaming","https://arxiv.org/abs/2202.03286","https://lilianweng.github.io/posts/2018-04-08-policy-gradient/#a2c","https://github.com/facebookresearch/ParlAI/tree/main/parlai/tasks/bot_adversarial_dialogue","https://lilianweng.github.io/posts/2021-01-02-controllable-text-generation/#nucleus","https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.09442","https://arxiv.org/abs/2202.03286","https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.15056","https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.14387","https://openai.com/blog/using-gpt-4-for-content-moderation","https://arxiv.org/abs/2308.04265","https://lilianweng.github.io/posts/2023-03-15-prompt-engineering/","https://arxiv.org/abs/2202.03286","https://arxiv.org/abs/2202.06675","https://github.com/notAI-tech/NudeNet)","https://perspectiveapi.com/","#peek-into-mitigation","#saddle-point-problem","https://arxiv.org/abs/1706.06083","#some-work-on-llm-robustness","https://assets.researchsquare.com/files/rs-2873090/v1_covered_3dc9af48-92ba-491e-924d-b13ba9b7216f.pdf?c=1686882819","https://arxiv.org/abs/2309.00614v2","#gradient-based-attacks","